{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7806","id":5214815134,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNtPDng","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7806","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7806.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7806.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7806","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7806/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7806/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7806/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/b8b514e3c978452f658f9c393c01c50be9540e07","number":7806,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(ci): scout classifier leg on the main-broken chain (#2176)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Implements the CI-failure classifier (scout) leg of issue #2176's failure-triage design on code's main-broken chain — queue task 13485.\n\n## What lands\n\n- **`scripts/classify_failure.py`** (new, stdlib-only): reads the log tails of a failed run's failing jobs and classifies the breakage as `quota-or-secret` / `infra-runner` / `infra-network` / `flake-suspect` / `real-regression` / `unknown`, emitting JSON with up to 5 evidence lines and a route. Rule order is part of the contract: quota/runner/network signals beat a generic failing-test summary from the same job.\n- **`main-broken.yml` scout step pair** between filing and remediation:\n  - classifies from the failing jobs' log tails and posts an `agent-note:v1` with the classification + evidence on the breakage issue **before any fix spend**;\n  - routing per the design: quota/secret → escalate (label + note naming the implicated credential, zero fix attempts); infra/flake → one automatic re-run of the failed jobs (`run_attempt` guard; a repeat escalates as infrastructure; third flake strike files a deduped flake-fix issue); real-regression/unknown → existing Jules/queue routing with the diagnosis attached;\n  - the `jules`-label step and the append-path fix-task dispatch now gate on the scout route (empty route = scout silence = previous behaviour, fail-open);\n  - `workflow_dispatch dry_run=true` prints the classification and files/sends nothing (the route step is create/append-only).\n- **Tests**: 18 contract tests in `scripts/tests/test_classify_failure.py` (one fixture family per class, rule-ordering, evidence cap, tail-window behaviour), wired into `scripts-test.yml`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `python3 -m unittest discover -s scripts/tests -p 'test_classify_failure.py'` — 18/18 pass on the laptop worktree.\n- `actionlint .github/workflows/main-broken.yml .github/workflows/scripts-test.yml` — clean.\n- Classifier CLI smoke test against a fabricated failed-job log dir + jobs manifest → `infra-network` / route `rerun` with the DNS line as evidence.\n- The live `workflow_dispatch dry_run=true` run against a known failed run can only execute once this workflow is on the default branch (GitHub dispatches the default-branch workflow definition); that is the first post-merge validation step.\n\nScope guardrails preserved: no `workflow_run` on `*`, per-breakage concurrency unchanged, scout authority limited to one re-run + comment/label/file within chain labels; it never edits code, merges, touches secrets, or disables workflows. Issue #2176 stays open (other jewels/bullets are separate packets).\n\nRefs #2176\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796761462&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7806&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7806&signature=97c188cdf0425fc9ca5c35e6fbb16d45d56a612b482b73cc083b6d1f031c6a0b\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7806?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **CI & Reliability**\n  * Failed checks are now categorized as infrastructure, intermittent, or code-related failures, with relevant log evidence captured for review.\n  * Infrastructure and intermittent failures can be rerun automatically; quota or secret-related failures can be escalated.\n  * Issues are routed based on failure type, and the fix queue is updated only when a fix task is queued.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-08T20:24:18Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T00:06:50Z","closed_at":"2026-11-09T00:06:24Z","merged_at":"2026-11-09T00:06:24Z","merge_commit_sha":"e5a4fdcbcb3f90b6552009420d900151454d9103","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[{"id":7767549,"node_id":"T_kwDOAZNvF84AdoX9","url":"https://api.github.com/organizations/26439447/team/7767549","members_url":"https://api.github.com/organizations/26439447/team/7767549/members{/member}","name":"codeowners","description":"Team Discussions: developing-today/code","permission":"pull","privacy":"closed","notification_setting":"notifications_enabled","html_url":"https://github.com/orgs/developing-today/teams/codeowners","repositories_url":"https://api.github.com/organizations/26439447/team/7767549/repos","slug":"codeowners","type":"organization","organization_id":26439447,"parent":null}],"head":{"label":"developing-today:queue/13485-2176-ci-classifier","ref":"queue/13485-2176-ci-classifier","repo":{"id":627308783,"node_id":"R_kgDOJWP47w","name":"code","full_name":"developing-today/code","owner":{"login":"developing-today","id":26439447,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjI2NDM5NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today/gists{/gist_id}","starred_ur